thread:
maria_sales: Quick heads-up — Orbis demo this morning. Streaming responses start then abruptly stop mid-payload. Customer saw JSON parse errors in their web client. They called it out during the sales call, we lost momentum :/

raj_se: ugh. do we have the client error text? Cc @jamie_eng

maria_sales: Copy from their console: `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at JSON.parse`

maria_sales: They also pasted the raw SSE fragment we sent: `data: {\"choices\":[{\"text\":\"Hello wo"}` — it looks truncated, no trailing newline/event boundary.

jamie_eng: That looks like the response stream is getting cut mid-chunk by an intermediary (proxy/edge). Could be nginx buffer or a keepalive/timeout on their side. Any proxy in front of their webview?

sam_cs: Orbis confirmed they're using an internal edge that rewrites some headers and has a 3s idle timeout on chunk writes.

raj_se: Ok, immediate workaround for the SDK: buffer until a full JSON object is received before JSON.parse, keep attempting reconnect on partial chunk, and expose a more forgiving retry for POC. We have a quick patch we can ship to them.

jamie_eng: Agree. Also want us to validate server side: ensure we flush full SSE events with `\n\n` and that Transfer-Encoding remains chunked. Can someone grab the Redwood server logs for that session id?

maria_sales: Session id: orbis-2026-03-21-77. I attached the transcript from their demo (they pasted it in the meeting chat).

oncall-bot: New request created: #INC-9937 — Investigate Orbis POC streaming cut mid-event. Assigned to jamie_eng. Link: https://redwood.incidents/INC-9937

jamie_eng: Pulling logs now. Quick grep shows `write()` calls sending 512 bytes then another write with 48 bytes — last write for the event got a 502 from their proxy during the second write: `upstream prematurely closed connection`

jamie_eng: Repro steps I used locally: curl -N to /v1/stream with a long response, then simulate nginx proxy with `proxy_buffering on; proxy_read_timeout 3s;` and I can reproduce mid-event truncation when chunks are delayed.

maria_sales: They asked about Dedicated too — they think if we run Dedicated it might eliminate proxy issues but they need to see reliability first. Pricing Q happened mid-call.

raj_se: For POC we should propose two parallel actions: 1) SDK patch to be defensive client-side (fast). 2) Ops change recommendation for their edge: disable proxy_buffering, increase proxy_read_timeout to 30s, and ensure keepalive/persistent connections (medium). If they want to move to Dedicated, it reduces our public LB hops but won't fix their internal edge rewrite.

sam_cs: Noted. Also capture a short doc for them so security doesn't block this: explain why chunked SSE is required and what headers must pass through unmodified (Transfer-Encoding, Connection, Content-Type).

maria_sales: I pinged Orbis dev: can you try the SDK patch and share a network HAR? They said yes and will run after lunch.

jamie_eng: Drafted quick SDK diff — whitespace only but logic to accumulate until a `\n`-terminated event or valid JSON parse succeeds. Example snippet:

```js
// pseudo
let buf = '';
source.on('data', chunk => {
  buf += chunk.toString('utf8');
  const events = buf.split(/\\n\\n/);
  buf = events.pop() || '';
  events.forEach(e => {
    if (!e) return;
    const dataLine = e.split('\\n').find(l => l.startsWith('data:'));
    if (!dataLine) return;
    try {
      const payload = JSON.parse(dataLine.replace(/^data:\\s*/, ''));
      deliver(payload);
    } catch (err) {
      // keep buffer until more data arrives
    }
  });
});
```

raj_se: Nice. Ship as 0.5.1-orpoc-hotfix and give them a CDN edge script if they need it.

maria_sales: Customer also wants a short blurb for their security team on risk profile of SSE vs websocket — can we draft one?

sam_cs: I'll draft a 1-paragraph security note: SSE is uni-directional from server to client, TLS-protected, relies on long-lived HTTP connection; main surface to harden is proxy/edge timeouts and header rewrites. Will attach by EOD.

jamie_eng: One more ops note: on Redwood side we can start emitting an event boundary marker header `X-Redwood-Event-End: true` after a full SSE event so if proxies try to inspect it's obvious. Not implemented yet but could help debugging.

maria_sales: Perfect. Next actions: (1) jamie ship SDK hotfix and test with Orbis HAR; (2) sam send security blurb and recommended proxy config; (3) raj update POC plan to include Dedicated pricing as an option but note it may not resolve internal edge rewrites.

raj_se: I'll update the proposal and call out expected ETA and costs. Scheduling pairing with Orbis devs for 16:00 PT to try the patch.

maria_sales: Thanks — please keep this thread updated. I'll escalate to AE if we need a contract tweak. :thumbsup:
